WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:06.791
At home at Gloucester Castle, Edmund moved ahead with his plan to win his father's inheritance.

2
00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:14.189
He had forged a letter, and when he saw his father approaching, he made a great show of quickly putting it in his pocket.

3
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.581
"What are you hiding?" asked the Earl of Gloucester.

4
00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:20.153
"It's nothing," replied his son.

5
00:00:20.154 --> 00:00:22.935
"Well, if it's nothing, why hide it?"

6
00:00:22.936 --> 00:00:29.856
Edmund pretended to be upset. "My lord, it's a letter from my brother. But I didn't want you to see it."

7
00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:34.889
"Give it to me," the earl ordered. He took the paper and began to read.

8
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:42.390
"What's this? Edgar doesn't want to wait until I die to inherit my estate and title!" sputtered Gloucester.

9
00:00:42.391 --> 00:00:49.011
"He wants me dead now, and then he will share his inheritance with you! Does he mean this?"

10
00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:54.433
"Sir, I hope not," said Edmund. "I'll speak with him to find out more."

11
00:00:54.434 --> 00:01:01.381
"How can he be such a monster when I love him so dearly?" Outraged, Gloucester strode away.

12
00:01:01.382 --> 00:01:05.810
Soon after, Edgar appeared. "Good day, brother," he said.

13
00:01:05.811 --> 00:01:09.904
"What have you done to upset our father?" asked Edmund.

14
00:01:09.905 --> 00:01:13.405
"I've done nothing!" Edgar replied, puzzled.

15
00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:19.255
"Well, he's so angry at you that I fear for your life!" Edmund exclaimed.

16
00:01:19.256 --> 00:01:25.911
"For now, you should avoid him. Go hide in my room, and carry a knife for safety."

17
00:01:25.912 --> 00:01:35.462
Edmund then promised to calm their father and arrange a meeting between the earl and Edgar that night. "I am on your side, brother," he lied.

18
00:01:35.463 --> 00:01:40.026
Meanwhile, Lear had settled into Goneril and Albany's castle.

19
00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:44.502
But Goneril had no patience for the old man and his knights.

20
00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:49.288
"They do nothing but cause trouble," she told her steward, Oswald.

21
00:01:49.289 --> 00:01:53.434
"When he returns from hunting, I don't want to see him.

22
00:01:53.435 --> 00:01:58.555
Tell him I'm sick. And I give you permission to ignore his demands.

23
00:01:58.556 --> 00:02:06.493
Tell the servants they don't have to always obey my father and his knights. If he doesn't like it, let him go to my sister's."

24
00:02:06.494 --> 00:02:14.168
When Lear returned, a man was waiting for him in the great hall of Goneril's castle. It was the loyal Earl of Kent.

25
00:02:14.169 --> 00:02:22.617
Rather than abandon his master, he had disguised himself as an ordinary servant so he could stay close and protect the king.

26
00:02:22.618 --> 00:02:27.673
Lear did not recognize him and asked, "Who are you? What do you want?"

27
00:02:27.674 --> 00:02:34.674
"I'm Caius. I'm honest, hardworking, and I want to serve you," replied Kent, bowing.

28
00:02:34.675 --> 00:02:38.810
"You seem to be a good fellow," said Lear. "Join my men."

29
00:02:38.811 --> 00:02:41.997
At that moment, Oswald appeared.

30
00:02:41.998 --> 00:02:50.444
"Where is my daughter?" asked Lear. But Oswald rudely left without replying. Lear was furious at this lack of respect.

31
00:02:50.445 --> 00:02:54.119
When Goneril finally entered the hall, she was frowning.

32
00:02:54.120 --> 00:03:02.024
"Father! You must get rid of half your knights. They drink and fight and make too much noise," she complained.

33
00:03:02.025 --> 00:03:08.557
"Oh, how sharper than a serpent's tooth it is to have a thankless child!" snapped Lear.

34
00:03:08.558 --> 00:03:16.124
"It is your servants who are rude and unhelpful! How can you treat me like this, after all I've done for you?"

35
00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:23.094
He turned to Kent and his knights. "Prepare to go to Regan's. Surely she'll be kinder!"

36
00:03:23.095 --> 00:03:33.024
Before Lear's knights even began to saddle their horses, Goneril sent a letter to Regan, warning her that Lear was being difficult and was headed to her castle.

37
00:03:33.025 --> 00:03:36.659
Regan decided to leave rather than deal with her father.

38
00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.976
So she and Cornwall went to visit the Earl of Gloucester.

39
00:03:40.977 --> 00:03:48.890
When Lear arrived at Regan's, he could not believe she had left. "Come, then," he ordered his men. "To Gloucester's!"

40
00:03:48.891 --> 00:03:58.827
At Gloucester Castle, Edmund met Edgar in the courtyard and pulled him aside, saying quietly, "Our father's servants know you're hiding in my room.

41
00:03:58.828 --> 00:04:05.844
It's best you leave now, under cover of night." Just then they saw their father entering the courtyard.

42
00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:12.821
"Forgive me," whispered Edmund, "but I must draw my sword so our father doesn't suspect I want to help you.

43
00:04:12.822 --> 00:04:16.604
Now take your knife and pretend to defend yourself."

44
00:04:16.605 --> 00:04:24.385
When Edmund saw their father and his servants approaching, he shouted at Edgar, "Yield! Explain yourself to our father!"

45
00:04:24.386 --> 00:04:33.093
Then, whispering again, he told Edgar to flee. After Edgar ran away, Edmund cut his own arm with his sword.

46
00:04:33.094 --> 00:04:37.856
"Edmund, where is your villainous brother?" cried Gloucester.

47
00:04:37.857 --> 00:04:47.442
"He's gone, Father. He wanted me to murder you! When I refused, he attacked me and then fled. Look, he has wounded me!"

48
00:04:47.443 --> 00:04:57.070
Gloucester went pale with shock. "I will ask Cornwall to order that Edgar be hunted down and put to death! You are my only son now."

49
00:04:57.071 --> 00:05:02.016
"My plan is working perfectly," thought Edmund with great glee.

50
00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:09.486
Just then trumpets sounded. Regan and Cornwall entered the courtyard, and Gloucester told them of Edgar's evil deeds.

51
00:05:09.487 --> 00:05:12.760
They praised Edmund for being so loyal.

52
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:16.323
Finally, Gloucester asked, "Why have you come?"

53
00:05:16.324 --> 00:05:21.944
"It's about my father. We need your advice," said Regan, flattering the earl.

54
00:05:21.945 --> 00:05:24.960
Gloucester bowed and led them inside.

55
00:05:24.961 --> 00:05:32.132
A few hours later, Lear arrived at Gloucester castle and asked to see his daughter and Cornwall.

56
00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:37.438
"I'm sorry," Gloucester told him, "they say they are tired and cannot see you."

57
00:05:37.439 --> 00:05:42.304
"They refuse to see me simply because they are tired?" shouted Lear.

58
00:05:42.305 --> 00:05:45.440
"Tell my daughter I command her to speak with me!"

59
00:05:45.441 --> 00:05:50.044
Gloucester left and soon returned with Regan and Cornwall.

60
00:05:50.045 --> 00:05:54.260
"Father, I am glad to see you," murmured Regan.

61
00:05:54.261 --> 00:05:58.483
"I should hope so," said Lear, "for are you not my daughter?

62
00:05:58.484 --> 00:06:03.770
Oh, beloved Regan, your sister Goneril has treated me shamefully!"

63
00:06:03.771 --> 00:06:09.207
"Father, you are judging Goneril too harshly," Regan replied coolly.

64
00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:16.119
"I'm sure my sister is being more than fair. Return to Goneril and ask for forgiveness."

65
00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:25.082
"Forgiveness for what? She wants to take away half my knights, and she's wounded my heart with her cruel words. Curses on your sister!"

66
00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:28.603
"Calm yourself, sir," chided Cornwall.

67
00:06:28.604 --> 00:06:35.286
"Father," Regan said, "your age is making you foolish. You must take my advice."

68
00:06:35.287 --> 00:06:42.160
"I will never return to your sister!" bellowed Lear. "Regan, surely, you are grateful for what I've done for you."

69
00:06:42.161 --> 00:06:47.471
Suddenly, the trumpets sounded again. In the doorway stood Goneril!

70
00:06:47.472 --> 00:06:52.482
"Goneril," said Lear, stunned, "are you not ashamed to look at me?"

71
00:06:52.483 --> 00:06:59.872
"Why should I be?" asked Goneril coldly. "What have I done wrong?" She walked over to Regan, who took her hand.

72
00:06:59.873 --> 00:07:05.142
"Father, I am not ready to care for you and all your men," said Regan.

73
00:07:05.143 --> 00:07:14.484
"Goneril is right—having too many people in one castle causes problems. Why not keep just 50 knights? Or even 25?"

74
00:07:14.485 --> 00:07:18.161
"Or why keep any?" Goneril added.

75
00:07:18.162 --> 00:07:22.773
"Indeed," said Regan. "Our own servants can look after you."

76
00:07:22.774 --> 00:07:28.909
Lear was wounded by his daughters' coldness. "Both of you have turned against me!" he cried.

77
00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:37.592
How small Cordelia's fault seems now. Oh, I must not weep! Instead, I shall take my revenge—!"

78
00:07:37.593 --> 00:07:44.749
A thunderclap drowned out his words as he strode through the castle gates. Rain began to pelt down.

79
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:50.226
"I don't know where he's going," said Gloucester, worried, "and there's no shelter close by."

80
00:07:50.227 --> 00:07:53.627
"It's his own fault," said Goneril.

81
00:07:53.628 --> 00:07:57.406
"And this will teach him a lesson," added Regan.

82
00:07:57.407 --> 00:08:01.891
"Regan is right. Lock your castle doors," barked Cornwall.

83
00:08:01.892 --> 00:08:08.251
A huge bolt of lightning lit up the sky. The storm was gathering force.

